# Build artifacts — the YAML is the code, these are outputs.
#
# The release ZIP and its checksum are NOT committed, and this is deliberate.
# SHA256SUMS.txt records the commit the artifact was built from; committing it
# changes that commit, which changes the recorded hash, which needs another
# commit. It never converges. A build output that names its own commit cannot
# live inside that commit.
#
# Rebuild either from the tag instead. It is reproducible -- timestamps are
# normalised, so a given tag always yields the same bytes and the same
# checksum:
#
#     bash scripts/build_release.sh v1.0.0
#
# The release DOCUMENTATION beside it is committed, because it is source.
dist/*/*.zip
dist/*/SHA256SUMS.txt
*.msapp
# EXCEPT the vendored donor -- a Microsoft MIT test asset the msapp build
# takes its format scaffolding from. See canvas-app/donor/README.md. The
# BUILT msapp in dist/canvas/ stays ignored like every other build output.
!canvas-app/donor/*.msapp
solution/bin/
solution/obj/
provisioning/schema.generated.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
